WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.682 --> 00:00:05.142
Eh, truth table with 3 letters, 8 rows, okay lah.

2
00:00:05.162 --> 00:00:08.662
But 20 letters? More than 1 MILLION rows.

3
00:00:08.682 --> 00:00:09.772
Who got time?

4
00:00:10.288 --> 00:00:12.428
DPLL is the smart way.

5
00:00:12.448 --> 00:00:15.708
It hunts for 1 model, and every step throws away a

6
00:00:15.728 --> 00:00:17.228
big chunk of the table.

7
00:00:17.248 --> 00:00:19.425
No need to fill in every row.

8
00:00:19.782 --> 00:00:23.309
Today, 4 things. The 1 move that DPLL makes.

9
00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:25.549
The 3 rules that pick the move.

10
00:00:25.569 --> 00:00:28.349
1 full trace by hand, exam style.

11
00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:31.549
And the pseudocode, which the exam prints with gaps, so must

12
00:00:31.569 --> 00:00:32.779
know by heart hor.

13
00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:38.544
DPLL eats clauses, so CNF first.

14
00:00:38.564 --> 00:00:41.464
The 1 move: make a literal TRUE.

15
00:00:41.484 --> 00:00:43.094
Then 2 things happen.

16
00:00:43.244 --> 00:00:48.014
Every clause that contains that literal is satisfied already: REMOVE it.

17
00:00:48.044 --> 00:00:52.304
Every clause that contains the opposite literal: that literal is dead,

18
00:00:52.324 --> 00:00:53.894
so SHORTEN the clause.

19
00:00:54.124 --> 00:00:57.894
Example: P false means not P is true.

20
00:00:58.044 --> 00:01:00.614
Clause not P or R: remove.

21
00:01:00.764 --> 00:01:03.694
Clause P or R: become just R.

22
00:01:03.726 --> 00:01:05.226
Which literal to pick?

23
00:01:05.246 --> 00:01:06.986
3 rules, in order.

24
00:01:07.006 --> 00:01:11.106
Rule 1, UNIT clause: a clause with only 1 literal.

25
00:01:11.126 --> 00:01:13.546
No choice what, must make it true.

26
00:01:13.566 --> 00:01:17.466
Rule 2, PURE literal: a letter that always show the same

27
00:01:17.486 --> 00:01:19.616
sign. Just make it true lor.

28
00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:24.346
Rule 3, SPLIT: no unit, no pure, then you choose.

29
00:01:24.366 --> 00:01:27.976
By hand: first letter in the alphabet, FALSE first.

30
00:01:28.176 --> 00:01:29.466
And when to stop?

31
00:01:29.486 --> 00:01:32.866
No clauses left: satisfiable, shiok.

32
00:01:32.886 --> 00:01:37.226
See Q and also not Q as unit clauses: contradiction, this

33
00:01:37.246 --> 00:01:38.856
branch die already.

34
00:01:41.064 --> 00:01:45.164
Now we trace. 5 clauses: not Q or not R.

35
00:01:45.184 --> 00:01:46.764
Not P or Q.

36
00:01:46.784 --> 00:01:49.564
P or R. Q or not R.

37
00:01:49.584 --> 00:01:52.128
Q or R. Got unit clause?

38
00:01:52.148 --> 00:01:56.528
No. Pure literal? No, every letter got both signs.

39
00:01:56.548 --> 00:01:59.008
So split: P FALSE first.

40
00:01:59.028 --> 00:02:01.208
Not P or Q: remove.

41
00:02:01.228 --> 00:02:03.568
P or R: shorten to R.

42
00:02:03.588 --> 00:02:06.888
Now 4 clauses, and R stand alone: unit!

43
00:02:06.908 --> 00:02:09.088
So R true. What is left?

44
00:02:09.108 --> 00:02:11.038
Not Q, and Q.

45
00:02:11.549 --> 00:02:15.651
Alamak, contradiction. Both cannot be true what.

46
00:02:15.671 --> 00:02:19.971
So BACKTRACK: go back to the original 5 clauses, this time

47
00:02:19.991 --> 00:02:23.051
P true. P or R: remove.

48
00:02:23.071 --> 00:02:25.651
Not P or Q: shorten to Q.

49
00:02:25.671 --> 00:02:27.971
Unit Q, so Q true.

50
00:02:27.991 --> 00:02:31.971
Only not R is left, unit again, so R false.

51
00:02:31.991 --> 00:02:34.735
No clauses left! Satisfiable.

52
00:02:34.755 --> 00:02:38.215
Model: P true, Q true, R false.

53
00:02:38.235 --> 00:02:41.842
Notice ah, R true came from the dead branch, throw away.

54
00:02:41.862 --> 00:02:44.455
The model comes from the branch that SURVIVED.

55
00:02:44.475 --> 00:02:46.775
And if P true also die?

56
00:02:46.795 --> 00:02:49.765
Then nothing left to try: unsatisfiable.

57
00:02:51.844 --> 00:02:53.904
Last part, the pseudocode.

58
00:02:53.924 --> 00:02:56.134
Same story, just written down.

59
00:02:56.164 --> 00:02:59.254
DPLL of F and literal.

60
00:02:59.284 --> 00:03:02.744
Line 1: remove clauses containing literal.

61
00:03:02.764 --> 00:03:06.384
Line 2: shorten clauses containing not literal.

62
00:03:06.404 --> 00:03:08.424
Mirror image, dun swap ah.

63
00:03:08.444 --> 00:03:12.864
Then 3 ifs. F contains no clauses: return TRUE.

64
00:03:12.884 --> 00:03:15.984
F contains empty clause: return FALSE.

65
00:03:16.004 --> 00:03:20.544
F contains a unit or pure L: return DPLL of F

66
00:03:20.564 --> 00:03:23.024
and L. Then the split.

67
00:03:23.044 --> 00:03:24.624
Choose P in F.

68
00:03:24.644 --> 00:03:28.664
If DPLL of F and not P: return true.

69
00:03:28.684 --> 00:03:32.224
Else: return DPLL of F and P.

70
00:03:32.244 --> 00:03:34.869
Not P first, that is your false first.

71
00:03:34.889 --> 00:03:39.029
The trap: no clauses and empty clause sound the same, but

72
00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:41.949
they are OPPOSITE. Empty set, you win.

73
00:03:41.969 --> 00:03:43.913
Empty clause, you lose.

74
00:03:43.933 --> 00:03:49.953
So remember: remove, shorten, unit, pure, split, false first.

75
00:03:49.973 --> 00:03:54.073
The practice notebook got 3 full traces, the pseudocode with gaps,

76
00:03:54.093 --> 00:03:56.753
and a small tracer to check every step.

77
00:03:56.773 --> 00:03:59.513
Graded work must be your own hor, the course does not

78
00:03:59.533 --> 00:04:01.703
allow AI there. Jia you!
